Chapter: ConstNarrowProven

 First slice of the bounds-prover reach campaign:
 a value expression built from
 literal-defined constants proves its range at a bounded store, so
 the CDX2051 silent-truncation warning is elided and the CDX2053
 proven info is reported instead. Covers the expression shapes the
 checker-side analysis recognizes — a constant name, an
 if-expression joining two constants, a let body, and a constant in
 ctor-payload and __record-set position. The deliberately unprovable
 store (a plain parameter) is rejected since CDX2051 became an error;
 its twin lives in errors/narrowing-unproven. The sidecars assert the
 proven diagnostic and the in-range runtime behavior.

Section: Constants

  code-a : Integer = 41

  code-b : Integer = 202

Section: Definitions

  Entry = record {
   code : Integer between 0 and 255
  }

  Wrapped =
   | MkWrapped (Integer between 0 and 255)

  unwrap : Wrapped -> Integer
  unwrap (w) = when w
   is MkWrapped (v) -> v

  make-direct : Boolean -> Entry
  make-direct (flag) = Entry { code = if flag then code-a else code-b }

  make-via-let : Integer -> Entry
  make-via-let (n) = Entry { code = let unused = n in code-a }

  set-code : Entry -> Entry
  set-code (e) = __record-set e "code" code-b

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((make-direct True).code))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((make-direct False).code))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((make-via-let 7).code))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text (unwrap (MkWrapped code-b)))
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((set-code (make-direct True)).code))
  end
